          "question": {
            "text": "If in a $\\triangle A B C, 2 b^2=a^2+c^2$, then $\\frac{\\sin 3B}{\\sin B}$ is equal to",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "FNNNx",
              "text": "\r\n$\\frac{c^2-a^2}{2 c a}$\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "sFOA1",
              "text": "\r\n$\\frac{c^2-a^2}{c a}$\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "ZpkJw",
              "text": "\r\n$\\frac{\\left(c^2-a^2\\right)^2}{(c a)^2}$\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "ipSID",
              "text": "\r\n$\\left[\\frac{c^2-a^2}{2 c a}\\right]^2$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "$\\frac{\\sin 3 B}{\\sin B}=\\frac{3 \\sin B-4 \\sin ^3 B}{\\sin B}$\r\n$=3-4 \\sin ^2 B$\r\n$=3-4\\left(1-\\cos ^2 B\\right)$\r\n$=-1+\\frac{4\\left(a^2+c^2-b^2\\right)^2}{4(a c)^2}$\r\n$=-1+\\frac{\\left(\\frac{a^2+c^2}{2}\\right)^2}{(a c)^2}$\r\n$=-1+\\frac{\\left(a^2+c^2\\right)^2}{4(a c)^2}$\r\n$=(\\frac{c^2-a^2}{2 a c})^2$",
            "image": null
          },
