          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 1,
          "question": {
            "text": "In a $\\triangle \\mathrm{ABC},$ if $\\frac{\\cos A}{\\mathrm{a}}=\\frac{\\cos \\mathrm{B}}{\\mathrm{b}}=\\frac{\\cos \\mathrm{C}}{\\mathrm{c}},$ and the side $\\mathrm{a}=2,$ then area of the triangle is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "g7ZlB",
              "text": "1",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "W5vTD",
              "text": "2",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "uP6QK",
              "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "N10iy",
              "text": "$\\sqrt{3}$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "$\\frac{\\cos A}{a}=\\frac{\\cos B}{b}=\\frac{\\cos C}{c}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{\\cos \\mathrm{A}}{2 \\mathrm{R} \\sin \\mathrm{A}}=\\frac{\\cos \\mathrm{B}}{2 \\mathrm{R} \\sin \\mathrm{B}}=\\frac{\\cos \\mathrm{C}}{2 \\mathrm{R} \\sin \\mathrm{C}}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\cot A=\\cot B=\\cot C$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{A}=\\mathrm{B}=\\mathrm{C}=60^{\\circ} \\Rightarrow \\Delta \\mathrm{ABC}$ is equilateral\r\n\r\nHence, area of $\\Delta=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\mathrm{a}^{2}=\\sqrt{3}$.",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
