          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "In a triangle $\\mathrm{ABC},$ if $\\mathrm{a}=2, \\mathrm{~B}=60^{\\circ}$ and $\\mathrm{C}=75^{\\circ}$, then b equals",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "kmlz2",
              "text": "$\\sqrt{3}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "0nXjS",
              "text": "$\\sqrt{6}$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "qZ24A",
              "text": "$\\sqrt{9}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "ZTCqf",
              "text": "$1+\\sqrt{2}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "$\\mathrm{A}=180^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}-75^{\\circ}=180^{\\circ}-135^{\\circ}=45^{\\circ}$\r\nNow, $\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{\\sin \\mathrm{A}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{b}}{\\sin \\mathrm{B}}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{2}{\\sin 45^{\\circ}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{b}}{\\sin 60^{\\circ}} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{b}=\\frac{2 \\cdot(\\sqrt{3} / 2)}{1 / \\sqrt{2}}=\\sqrt{6}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
          "questionStructure": [
            "default"
          ],
