      "title": "Cosine Rule and Projection Formula",
      "totalQuestions": 1,
      "questions": [
        {
          "_id": "64c0e7d36f5bfc7ab78ae82b",
          "previousYearPapers": [
            {
              "_id": "61a8bf0fc821b6514e527d79",
              "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
              "heldOn": "2015-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
              "isVisible": true,
              "shortName": "2015",
              "title": "BITSAT 2015"
            }
          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "In a $\\triangle A B C$, the lengths of the two larger sides are 10 and 9 units, respectively. If the angles are in $\\mathrm{AP}$, then the length of the third side can be",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "FEeiK",
              "text": "$5 \\pm \\sqrt{6}$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3lvdY",
              "text": "$3 \\sqrt{3}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "omNsO",
              "text": "$\\underline{5}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "wqGEc",
              "text": "None of these",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Let A, B and $C$ be the three angles of $\\Delta A B C$ and Let $a=10$ and $b=9$ It is given that the angles are in $\\mathrm{AP}$. $\\therefore 2 \\mathrm{~B}=\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{C}$ on adding $\\mathrm{B}$ both the sides,\r\n\r\nwe get\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n3 \\mathrm{~B}=\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{B}+\\mathrm{C} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow 3 \\mathrm{~B}=180^{\\circ} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{B}=60^{\\circ}\r\n\r\n\\end{array}\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nNow, we know $\\cos \\mathrm{B}=\\frac{\\mathrm{a}^{2}+\\mathrm{c}^{2}-\\mathrm{b}^{2}}{2 \\mathrm{ac}}$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow \\cos 60^{\\circ}=\\frac{10^{2}+\\mathrm{c}^{2}-9^{2}}{2 \\times 10 \\times \\mathrm{c}} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{100+\\mathrm{c}^{2}-81}{20 \\mathrm{c}} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{c}^{2}-10 \\mathrm{c}+19=0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{c}=5 \\pm \\sqrt{6}\r\n\r\n\\end{array}\r\n\r\n$$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
